===Dependent, disputed, or restricted territories===
Visa requirements for Turkish citizens for visits to various territories, disputed areas, partially recognized countries and restricted zones:

;Africa
*{{flag|Eritrea}} (outside [[Asmara]]) — Visa covers [[Asmara]] only; to travel in the rest of the country, a Travel Permit for Foreigners is required (20 [[Eritrean nakfa]]).<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.eritrea.be/MoT.htm|title=Ministry of Tourism - Tourism Service Center|first=Hans van der|last=Splinter|website=www.eritrea.be|access-date=17 July 2017}}</ref>
*{{flag|Sahrawi Arab Democratic Republic}} ([[Free Zone (region)|Western Sahara controlled territory]]) — Visa not required up to 3 months.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/western-sahara/entry-requirements|title=Entry requirements - Western Sahara travel advice - GOV.UK|website=www.gov.uk|access-date=17 July 2017}}</ref>
*{{flag|Somaliland}} — Visa issued on arrival (30 days for 30 [[USD]], payable on arrival also permission from the federal government of Somalia is required).<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.slimmigration.com/visa-section/ | title=Types Of Somaliland Visa}}</ref>
*{{flag|Sudan}} — All foreigners traveling more than 25 kilometers outside of [[Khartoum]] must obtain a travel permit.<ref name="travel.state.gov">{{cite web|url=https://travel.state.gov/content/passports/english/country/sudan.html|title=Sudan|website=travel.state.gov|access-date=17 July 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150905120352/http://travel.state.gov/content/passports/english/country/sudan.html|archive-date=5 September 2015|url-status=dead}}</ref>
*{{flagicon|Sudan}} [[Darfur]] — Separate travel permit is required.<ref name="travel.state.gov"/>

;Asia
*{{flag|Hong Kong}} — Visa not required for 90 days.<ref>{{Timatic|nationality=TR|destination=HK}}</ref>
*{{flag|India}} — Protected Area Permit (PAP) required for whole states of [[Nagaland]] and [[Sikkim]] and parts of states [[Mizoram]], [[Manipur]], [[Arunachal Pradesh]], [[Uttaranchal]], [[Jammu and Kashmir (union territory)|Jammu and Kashmir]], [[Rajasthan]], [[Himachal Pradesh]]. Restricted Area Permit (RAP) required for all of [[Andaman and Nicobar Islands]] and parts of [[Sikkim]]. Some of these requirements are occasionally lifted for a year.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.timaticweb.com/cgi-bin/tim_website_client.cgi?FullText=1&COUNTRY=IN&SECTION=VI&SUBSECTION=00&user=KLMB2C&subuser=KLMB2C |title=Visa information |website=www.timaticweb.com |access-date=3 February 2022 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20140314003632/https://www.timaticweb.com/cgi-bin/tim_website_client.cgi?FullText=1&COUNTRY=IN&SECTION=VI&SUBSECTION=00&user=KLMB2C&subuser=KLMB2C |archive-date=14 March 2014 |url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://arunachaltourism.com/entry_formalities.php |title=Arunachal Tourism |access-date=2014-08-01 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140701111837/http://arunachaltourism.com/entry_formalities.php |archive-date=2014-07-01 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://lakshadweeptourism.nic.in/web9.htm |title=Tourism in Lakshadweep |access-date=2014-08-01 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140713171604/http://lakshadweeptourism.nic.in/web9.htm |archive-date=2014-07-13 }}</ref>
*{{flag|Kazakhstan}} — Special permission required for the town of [[Baikonur]] and surrounding areas in [[Kyzylorda Oblast]], and the town of [[Gvardeyskiy, Kazakhstan|Gvardeyskiy]] near [[Almaty]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://travel.state.gov/content/passports/english/country/kazakhstan.html|title=Kazakhstan|website=travel.state.gov|access-date=17 July 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150905125509/http://travel.state.gov/content/passports/english/country/kazakhstan.html|archive-date=5 September 2015|url-status=dead}}</ref>
*{{flagicon|Iran}} [[Kish Island]] — Visitors to [[Kish Island]] do not require a visa.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://blog.rimazrauf.com/flying-to-kish-island-from-dubai-for-visa-change/ |title=Flying to Kish Island from Dubai for visa change. - Rimaz Rauf Blog |access-date=2014-12-17 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150120172555/http://blog.rimazrauf.com/flying-to-kish-island-from-dubai-for-visa-change/ |archive-date=2015-01-20 |url-status=dead }}</ref>
*{{flag|Macao}} — Visa not required for 30 days.<ref>{{Timatic|nationality=TR|destination=MO}}</ref>
*{{flagicon|Malaysia}} [[Sabah]] and [[Sarawak]] — These states have their own immigration authorities and passport is required to travel to them, however the same visa applies.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://travel.state.gov/content/passports/english/country/malaysia.html|title=Malaysia|website=travel.state.gov|access-date=17 July 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150905131025/http://travel.state.gov/content/passports/english/country/malaysia.html|archive-date=5 September 2015|url-status=dead}}</ref>
*{{flag|North Korea}} outside [[Pyongyang]] – People are not allowed to leave the capital city, tourists can only leave the capital with a governmental tourist guide (no independent moving)
*{{flag|Palestine}} — Visa not required. Arrival by sea to [[Gaza Strip]] not allowed.<ref>{{Timatic|nationality=TR|destination=PS}}</ref>
*{{flagicon|Saudi Arabia}} [[Mecca]] and [[Medina]] — Non-Muslims and those following the [[Ahmadiyya]] religious movement are strictly prohibited from entry.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.saudia.com/pages/before-flying/travel-information/hajj-and-umrah | title=Hajj and Umrah Tourist Visas | website=www.saudia.com | language=en | access-date=2017-06-13}}</ref>
*{{flag|Taiwan}} — eVisa.<ref>{{Timatic|nationality=TR|destination=TW}}</ref>
*{{Flagicon|Tajikistan}} [[Gorno-Badakhshan Autonomous Province]] — OIVR permit required (15+5 [[Tajikistani Somoni]]) and another special permit (free of charge) is required for [[Lake Sarez]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.pamirs.org/visas.htm|title=Pamirs - the roof of the world|website=www.pamirs.org|access-date=17 December 2014|archive-date=30 June 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170630035659/http://www.pamirs.org/visas.htm|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.traveltajikistan.com/visas/gbao.html |title=Travel Tajikistan - Permit to visit Gorno-Badakhshan Autonomous Oblast (GBAO) |access-date=2014-08-01 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150423031531/http://www.traveltajikistan.com/visas/gbao.html |archive-date=2015-04-23 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://tajiktourism.com/tajikistan-visa/|title=Tajikistan Visa|date=19 April 2012|access-date=17 July 2017|archive-date=6 July 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170706121812/http://tajiktourism.com/tajikistan-visa/|url-status=dead}}</ref>
*{{flag|Turkmenistan}} — A special permit, issued prior to arrival by Ministry of Foreign Affairs, is required if visiting the following places: [[Atamurat]], [[Cheleken]], [[Dashoguz]], [[Serakhs]] and [[Serhetabat]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.timaticweb.com/cgi-bin/tim_website_client.cgi?FullText=1&COUNTRY=TM&SECTION=VI&SUBSECTION=AI&user=KLMB2C&subuser=KLMB2C |title=Visa information |website=www.timaticweb.com |access-date=3 February 2022 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20140314003610/https://www.timaticweb.com/cgi-bin/tim_website_client.cgi?FullText=1&COUNTRY=TM&SECTION=VI&SUBSECTION=AI&user=KLMB2C&subuser=KLMB2C |archive-date=14 March 2014 |url-status=dead}}</ref>
*{{flagicon|People's Republic of China}} [[Tibet Autonomous Region]] — Tibet Travel Permit required (10 [[US Dollars]]).
<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.tibettravelplanner.com/travel_permit.htm|title=How to get a Tibet Travel Permits - Tibet Visa 2016?|website=www.tibettravelplanner.com|access-date=17 July 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171022061211/http://www.tibettravelplanner.com/travel_permit.htm|archive-date=22 October 2017|url-status=dead}}</ref>
*{{flagicon|United Nations}} [[Korean Demilitarized Zone]] — restricted zone.
*{{flagicon|United Nations}} [[UNDOF Zone]] and [[Ghajar]] — restricted zones.
*{{flagicon|Vietnam}} [[Phú Quốc]] — can visit without a visa for up to 30 days.<ref name="vietseatourist.vn"/>
*{{flag|Yemen}} — Special permission needed for travel outside [[Sanaa]] or [[Aden]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://travel.state.gov/content/passports/english/country/yemen.html|title=Yemen|website=travel.state.gov|access-date=17 July 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150905120633/http://travel.state.gov/content/passports/english/country/yemen.html|archive-date=5 September 2015|url-status=dead}}</ref>

