arctica.gov.au/living-and-working/predeparture/expeditioner-engagement-information|title=Forms expeditioners must sign|website=www.antarctica.gov.au|access-date=17 July 2017|archive-date=27 November 2012|archive-url=https://archive.today/20121127122832/https://www.antarctica.gov.au/living-and-working/predeparture/expeditioner-engagement-information|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.heardisland.aq/about/frequently-asked-questions#visit_heard_island|title=Frequently asked questions|first=c=AU;o=Commonwealth of Australia;ou=Department of the Environment and Energy;ou=Australian Antarctic|last=Division|website=www.heardisland.aq|date=28 February 2005 |access-date=17 July 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.npolar.no/en/antarctica/peter-I-oy.html |title=Peter I Øy - Norwegian Polar Institute |access-date=May 12, 2014 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131017215217/http://www.npolar.no/en/antarctica/peter-I-oy.html |archive-date=October 17, 2013 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.npolar.no/en/antarctica/dronning-maud-land.html |title=Dronning Maud Land - Norwegian Polar Institute |access-date=August 20, 2011 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131017215832/http://www.npolar.no/en/antarctica/dronning-maud-land.html |archive-date=October 17, 2013}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.mfat.govt.nz/Foreign-Relations/Antarctica/3-New-Zealand-Procedures-for-Visitors-to-Antarctica/index.php |title=Antarctica - NZ Procedures for Non-Governmental Visitors to Antarctica: NZ Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Trade |access-date=17 December 2014 |archive-date=22 May 2010 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100522033603/http://www.mfat.govt.nz/Foreign-Relations/Antarctica/3-New-Zealand-Procedures-for-Visitors-to-Antarctica/index.php |url-status=dead}}</ref>
